  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nAs of 3 AM Friday morning, midlevel ridging continues across the \neastern 2/3rds of the CONUS with troughing near the west coast. This \ncontinues to result in the unseasonably hot stretch of weather \nacross the central Plains. Temperatures this afternoon will once \nagain surge through the 90s and into the low 100s for most \nlocations. Factoring in surface dew points in the mid to upper 60s \nwill produce heat indices around 105. Transitioning into the weekend \nand into next week, the midlevel ridge is progged to amplify across \nthe southern and central Plains as an omega block pattern emerges. \nThis will keep the forecast area dry and unseasonably hot. Mid \nto long range guidance suggests the midlevel ridge may briefly \nweaken during the second half of next week as a shortwave trough\nejects across the northern states. This may push a cold front \ntowards central and southern KS with the possibility of cooler \ntemperatures and rain chances. That being said, long range \nguidance then amplifies the ridge across the central Plains by \nnext weekend (September 12-13).",
